    "agent_last_message": "Implemented a standalone C++20 project in [output/CMakeLists.txt](/workspace/output/CMakeLists.txt) and [output/main.cpp](/workspace/output/main.cpp). The tool accepts `--input` and `--output`, streams the input file in binary mode for byte-accurate `characters` counting, computes `lines` per the spec\u2019s newline rules, treats words as maximal non-whitespace byte sequences, folds words to lowercase for frequency counting, sorts `top_words` by descending count then ascending lexicographic order, writes the required JSON shape, and returns `0`/`1`/`2` with explicit invalid-invocation vs internal-error handling.\n\nI verified it by building with `cd /workspace/output && cmake -B build && cmake --build build`, then checking exact output for empty input, no trailing newline, trailing newline, whitespace-only input, tie ordering in `top_words`, and invalid invocation cases. The built binary is at `output/build/wordcount`.",
